WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:05.850
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:13.390
The reading from the Sinaxadion, for July 21st, on which we commemorate our righteous

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:22.930
Father Simeon of Homs, full for Christ's sake and his companion, John.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:28.730
On the 21st of the month, we celebrate the memory of our venerable Father Simeon of

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:37.110
Emesa, the full for Christ, and John, his companion in Askeesys.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:43.750
Saints Simeon and John were from Syria and lived during the reign of Justinian.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:51.990
John, at the age of 22, had just married, and Simeon, two years older, only had his

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:58.310
old mother for family. Finding a bond of friendship while on a pilgrimage to the

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:05.230
holy places that they had undertaken for the feast of the exaltation of the cross,

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:09.510
they decided to continue to travel together.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:16.150
When they arrived in the region of Jericho, John told his companion that the men who lived

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:22.830
in the monasteries near the Jordan were like angels of God, and pointing towards the road

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:30.390
that led there, he said, this is the road that leads to life.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:40.740
Then indicating the great highway he added, and this is the road that leads to death.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.340
After having prayed and drawn lots about the road they should take, they went to the monastery

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:53.340
of St. Yerassimos with great joy, forgetting all that binds to the world.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:59.980
The abbot of the monastery, blessed Nikon, had been given a revelation concerning the arrival

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:07.580
of the two young men, and he met them at the door to welcome them, and exhort them to renunciation,

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:13.460
prophesying what would be their future way of life.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:23.100
At their request, Nikon answered them immediately, and clothed them in the holy monastic habit, introducing

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:28.060
them to a new life by a second baptism.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:34.060
Fearful, however, of losing the divine zeal that burned in their hearts, and the resplendent

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:40.900
glory that they had seen on the monastic habit, they decided two days later to leave the

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:50.180
monastery and go apart from all men to live in the desert abandoned to providence.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:55.780
They directed their steps toward the dead sea, and arrived in a part of the desert called

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:03.060
Aranonas, where they found some buildings and supplies left by a hermit who had died a few

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.420
days earlier.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:11.700
But as soon as they began their ascetic endeavors in solitude, they were assailed by the memory

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:19.060
of their dear ones, John of his wife, and Simeon of his mother.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:26.180
After pressure from these thoughts and the trials of Sloth, Asidia, they were close to abandoning

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.980
their struggle.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:33.700
But every time the memory of the effulgent glory that they had seen over the monastic habit

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:40.980
and the appearing of their spiritual father in a dream gave them courage to persevere.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:48.100
They lived in cells, a stone's throw from each other, and when they were overwhelmed by temptation

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.740
or sloth, they met to pray together.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:58.900
They then recounted their visions to each other and rejoiced to be delivered by God from preoccupation

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:07.060
with their kinsfolk in order to persevere night and day in undistracted prayer.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:14.660
They thus made such progress that in a very few years they were counted worthy to be visited

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:20.980
by God and receive the gift of working miracles.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:27.140
After spending thirty years in the desert exposed to the rigors of the climate and the innumerable

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:34.340
machinations of the devil, Simeon, who had attained blessed impossibility through the grace of the

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:41.380
Holy Spirit who dwelt in him, suggested to his companion that he himself leave the desert

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:48.580
in order to save others by exposing the foolishness of the world by the power of Christ.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:54.740
John, believing that Simeon was the victim of demonic delusion,

00:04:54.740 --> 00:05:01.620
admonished him and reminded him of the promise that they had both made never to be separated.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:10.180
But no argument could overcome Simeon's resolution and believing that his decision came from divine

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:18.500
inspiration. John let him go after having made him promise that they would meet again before leaving

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:26.260
this life. Simeon first made a pilgrimage to Jerusalem. Once after having prayed for three days in

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:35.220
the holy places, he left for Emesa, having decided to feign folly to carry out his ministry of salvation.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:42.580
He was thus the first to embrace this perilous askees of folly for Christ,

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:51.220
applying literally the words of the Apostle. If any man among you seem to be wise in this world,

00:05:52.020 --> 00:06:00.660
let him become a fool that he may be wise. His whole purpose was to save souls either through

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:08.180
ridiculous behavior and calculated artifices, or by the miracles that he worked in offering himself

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:15.460
to derision and contempt, or by the teaching and prophetic words that he spoke while feigning folly.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:24.820
In all this, he strove to remain hidden and unknown to men in order to flee their praise and honor,

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:33.780
living in the world as though in the desert. He made his entrance into the town, dragging,

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:42.980
on a rope tied to his belt, a dead dog, which he had found on a pile of manure and pursued by a

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:51.780
mocking gang of schoolchildren. The next day, being a Sunday, he went into the church and began to

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:59.860
put out the candles, throwing nuts on the flames. When they tried to chase him out, he stepped onto

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:08.580
the ambon and bombarded the women with nuts. Finally thrown out, he overturned the tables of the

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:16.100
pastry-maker who beat him up. A fritter-seller had pity on him and suggested to Simeon that he

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:24.580
look after his booth. But Simeon set to giving away his merchandise to passers-by and greedily eating

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:32.180
the fritters as he had been fasting for a week, warned by his wife the merchant belabored him and

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:42.420
drove him away. That evening, Simeon took a bare handful of burning charcoal and lit incense on it.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:50.900
But, as soon as a merchant's wife saw him, he, pretending to be burned, put the embers in his coat,

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:58.980
which also took no harm. Later on, he brought about the conversion of the merchant,

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:08.390
who was a disciple of Severius of Antioch, by driving out a demon. Simeon then entered the

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:14.870
service of a tavernkeeper, who showed himself cruel and pitiless toward him, although the saint's

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:23.030
buffoonery gave him more trade. One day, he punished Simeon harshly for having broken a pint

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:30.710
jug of wine. But when he himself saw a snake had released its venom in the wine, he broke all the

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:38.550
rest of the crockery in trying to kill the reptile. From that time, looked on as a saint by his

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:46.390
patron, Simeon pretended to want to dishonor the merchant's wife, and the latter, alerted by his wife's

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:56.940
cries, drove him away with blows. The man of God lived right in the town, impassable, and is

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:03.660
though free of the cares of the flesh, and the conventions of modesty, relieving himself in the

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:12.540
street, going naked into the part of the public baths reserved for women. His clothes wrapped round

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:20.060
his head, dancing with actresses whose hands he held, or playing with prostitutes, without feeling

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:27.900
the slightest carnal stirring, and keeping his spirit imperturbably occupied with the work of God.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:37.500
He used this strategy to make the acquaintance of loose women, and secretly promised them a large

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:46.300
sum of money if they would keep chaste. When he learned that one of his friends had fallen back into

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:54.860
luxury, he punished her either with a sickness, or by allowing a demon to torment her. He had also

00:09:54.860 --> 00:10:03.900
received the grace of abstinence, and spent the great fast without eating anything. When great Thursday

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:10.860
came, though, he sat at a pastry-maker's stall and devoured cream cakes to the great scandal of the

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:20.940
bigoted. On other occasions, after having spent the week in fasting, he ate meat in public. One day,

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:28.940
he began throwing stones at some passersby who were meaning to go down a haunted road, thus preserving

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:35.820
them from perdition. Another time he afflicted some young girls who were jeering at him with a squint,

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:44.300
and then healed some of them by kissing their eyes, but left the others in that state, as he saw

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:51.500
that they would otherwise fall into debauchery. On Sundays, he stood at the church door

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:58.620
eating sausages that he had wrapped round his shoulders like a deacon's stall, holding in his left

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:07.500
hand a pot of mustard with which he painted the mouths of any who mocked at him. He healed a peasant

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:14.780
who had been struck with blindness after stealing goats from his neighbor by coating his eyes with mustard.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:22.620
He once paralyzed the hand of a trickster by throwing a stone at him and then healed him by appearing

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:30.380
to him in a vision and making him promise to abandon his trade. Yet another time he began beating the

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:37.980
pillars of the school with a whip, thus predicting the earthquake that would soon destroy the city of

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:48.780
Antioch in the year 588. And when the quake took place, the pillars that he had whipped remained

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:56.860
standing. Before an epidemic of plague, he embraced all the children who were to become its victims,

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:06.140
wishing them a good journey. He often went into the houses of the wealthy, practicing his usual

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:13.260
buffoonery and pretending to embrace the women servants. One of them, having accused him of getting

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:21.420
her with child, Simeon took care of the woman during her pregnancy, but she was unable to give birth

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:31.340
until she had revealed the name of the real father. The Holy Fools solicitude extended to everyone,

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:39.180
especially the possessed, of whom he healed a great many by his prayer after having pretended to be like

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:48.540
them. A Jewish artisan saw him one day flanked by two angels. He wanted to reveal the saint's secret,

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:57.180
but Simeon appeared to him in a dream and set a seal on his mouth. The same thing happened to all who

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:06.460
discovered his virtue. They found themselves incapable of spreading it abroad. By means of all these

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:13.980
prophetic acts and public harangs in his simulation of folly, Saint Simeon, who always addressed and treated

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:23.100
men as fools, or mindless, denounced the crimes of some and the thefts and debauchery of others,

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:30.780
thus bringing the habit of sin to an end through almost the whole town of Emisa.

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:38.940
Possessing nothing in this world, he spent all his nights in prayer in a dilapidated hut,

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:47.100
but he left each morning after having bathed the earth with tears for the salvation of his brethren.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:54.700
He then went into the town, his head crowned with an olive branch and holding a twig in his hand,

00:13:55.340 --> 00:14:03.580
dancing and crying out, victory for the emperor and for the town. He signified by these words,

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:10.220
the victory acquired by the intellect and by his soul in the striving of prayer.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:18.460
God had also allowed his hair and beard not to grow during all his years in Emisa,

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:24.700
so that he was deprived of the respect accorded to monks by their outward appearance.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:33.660
He only spoke rationally with a deacon called John, whose son he had saved from a false accusation

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:42.460
of murder. At these times a delightful fragrance came from his mouth, but he threatened his interlocutor

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:47.660
with terrible torments in the future life if he devolged his secret.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:53.660
When he had finished his course two days before leaving this life,

00:14:54.380 --> 00:15:00.540
Simeon recounted his life to the deacon and revealed to him that in fulfillment of the promise

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:06.940
that they had made to each other, he had seen in a vision his companion John the ascetic,

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:14.700
with a crown on his head, bearing the words, the crown of patience in the desert.

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:24.380
And John had replied that he, Simeon, would wear the crown of all the souls he had saved by his

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:32.300
buffoonery. After having exhorted the deacon to mercy and never to approach the holy sanctuary

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:39.580
with evil thoughts in his heart against anyone, he took leave of him. He retired to his hut,

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:47.660
and not wanting to become an object of wonder by his death, he slid under a pile of wood,

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:52.620
but always lay there so that it would look as though he had been crushed to death.

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:58.220
As those who knew him well had not seen him in the town for a couple of days,

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.980
they went to his hut and found him dead.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:09.180
Believing that he had been the victim of an accident, they did not even bother to wash the body,

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:15.980
but buried him with neither candles nor hymns in the cemetery reserved for foreigners.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:23.500
When the cortege passed by the house of a Jewish glass-blower who had been converted by Simeon,

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:32.460
the Jew heard such salmity has had never been heard on earth, sung by a vast but invisible crowd.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:41.420
Stupified, he looked through the window and saw just two men, caring the remains of the man of God.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:51.500
He then cried out, blessed are you, you fool, because deprived of the accompaniment of human salmity,

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:59.820
you have the heavenly powers honoring you with their hymns, and he went and buried him with his own hands.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:07.660
When Deacon John learned of the saint's death, he went to the cemetery and opened the grave,

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:16.780
but he found it empty and realized that the Lord had glorified his servant by taking him to glory in

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:25.100
the body before the general resurrection. It was only thus that the people of Emesa understood

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:33.740
that a new apostle had lived among them to bring about their salvation while remaining hidden.

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:42.700
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's O Lord Jesus Christ our God have mercy on us and save us.
